# Actual evidence and limits

One bounded dense author sanity run completed at 2026-10-15T23:45:42Z with return code 0 and empty stderr. The executed source is finite_check.at_launch.py, SHA256 `317e24380e9f3c942d5a10c667c3c484ccf3108d69979cbc52799def5ba5dab5`, 5,153 bytes. CHECK_LAUNCH.json and CHECK_RESULT.json preserve the command, actual interpreter, timestamps, launcher identity and unchanged after-run source hash. Raw complete streams are finite_check.stdout.log and finite_check.stderr.log. The entire stdout was inspected, including its final empty failures list; an exit code alone was not treated as verification.

The executable builds full physical qubit matrices directly, with no imported theorem implementation. It used NumPy 2.4.4 and SciPy 1.17.1, twelve prescribed cases with N=2–6 source qubits, and total Hilbert dimension at most 128. It checked the installed scalar, resonance commutator, exact bare-corrector identity, full ferromagnetic gap against the lower bound, collective fluctuation formula, and 36 complete-isometry observations at s=0,0.1,0.2. Cases include a negative source frequency with its actual positive reserve and a pure Z target. All finite checks had no recorded failure. The largest displayed corrector-identity residual was about 6.04e-15. The run's measured internal elapsed time was 0.132 seconds rounded upward; the launcher allowed 180 seconds and the source included a 120-second internal wall-time guard.

These finite floating-point checks are author checks, not independent machinery or proof. They do not instantiate the asymptotic epsilon recipe (whose source sizes are much larger), prove the arbitrary-N gap, verify a native state supplier, solve the general bus equations, or verify the general reduction's spectral premise. No full-reference density matrix was sampled: the checked 2-column isometry norm covers all old-qubit inputs and passive references mathematically, subject to floating-point accuracy. The analytic proof provides the general claim; an independent checker remains necessary before acceptance.

Other execution is metadata only: capture_sources.py checks supplied hashes and copies exact sources; freeze.py records final identities. No compiler search, canonical runner/cache/graph update, external network/literature use, Git/PR operation, audit, lock, axiom or editable-prompt change occurred. No agents were spawned and no other worker science was inspected.
